; Page text with one bad line per defect, each beside its corrected form. Every
; bad line is reported and no good line is. Lines starting with ';' are not
; published, so this one may say "The iron shield ($2C) is in levels 3, 8, 14,
; 20" freely.
;
; Bad, and the defect each one shows:
;   a code beside a name, and a list of the levels holding it
;   a code list, and facts about the level data
;   a page heading in storage vocabulary that counts its contents
;   a definition framed as progress
;   a definition carrying the logic that changes the value
;   a glossary entry for a category of program symbol
;   a table cell ending a noun phrase in a full stop
;   a dimension with ASCII x
; One more, the same code in parentheses on four surfaces: a heading, a
; paragraph, a table cell and a glossary title.
[Page:Levels]
PageContent=#INCLUDE(LevelsContent)

[LevelsContent]
<h2 class="ref-section" id="all">The 50 records</h2>

<h2 class="ref-section" id="cards">Level by level</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
The iron shield ($2C) is in the scripts of levels 3, 8, 14, 20. Rock rain
is in those of 41, 43, 47, 50, 58.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
The iron shield turns a shot back where it strikes.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
No level places $06, $1A or $3C.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
Level 50 has no empty cell.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
9 slots hold $00.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
Each card shows the level's room layout and the enemies its wave script can
send.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
A 2x2-character block, a 16x16-pixel tile.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
A 2×2-character block, a 16×16-pixel tile.
</div>

#TABLE(default)
{ =h Table | =h Record | =h What the record holds }
{ #R$CC00 | 48 bytes | The 8×6 grid of room tile codes, row-major. }
{ #R$CC30 | 48 bytes | The 8×6 grid of room tile codes, row-major }
TABLE#

<h2 class="ref-section" id="wall">Wall ($40–$7F)</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
A wall ($40–$7F) stands in a slot until a bomb clears it.
</div>

#TABLE(default)
{ =h Thing | =h What it is }
{ wall | A wall ($40–$7F) of any design }
{ wall | A wall of any design }
TABLE#

[Page:Glossary]
SectionPrefix=Term

[Term:level_index:Level index]
How far the player has got, 0 to 49. It wraps back to 0, so the level set
repeats.

[Term:level_index_2:Level index]
After the fiftieth level it wraps back to 0, so the level set repeats.

[Term:level_index_good:Level index]
Which level is being played, counted from 0.

[Term:constants:Constants]
The names in operands. Each stands for one address or size.

[Term:redraw_flag:Redraw flag]
A flag on one screen cell saying its picture has changed since the screen was
last drawn.

[Term:wall:Wall ($40–$7F)]
A block in the room that a bomb can break.

[Poke:enemy_speed:Enemy speeds above 6]
POKE 47904 ($BB20) with the new limit. The decimal is what the reader types.

[Page:Tiles]
[TilesContent]
<div class="paragraph">
Not a wall ($20–$3F, or $80 and up): passable. The tile map ($B200) holds codes.
</div>

[Page:Siblings]
[SiblingsContent]
<div class="paragraph">
IDs $20–$3F are passable.
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
Headings 0–3 move it 2 px left instead.
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
The headings sit 45° apart.
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
Test Y = sprite Y moved -2 px, upward.
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
The drone skips the speed limit. Nine of the 50 wave scripts carry it.
</div>
